* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary

# The offline build is a byte-exact artefact, not source.
#
# CI proves it is current by rebuilding and diffing, which only works if git
# stores exactly what the build wrote rather than a normalised version of it.
#
# Note the sharp edge, because it has drawn blood once: `text=auto` above keeps
# every *source* file LF in the index no matter what an editor does to the
# working copy, which means a stray CRLF in the working tree is invisible to
# `git status`. This folder is exempt from that normalisation, so a build that
# copies bytes out of the working tree can carry the invisible CRLF straight in
# here, where it is preserved and shows up as spurious drift. The build now
# normalises line endings itself and refuses to emit a carriage return, which is
# the guard that actually holds — not this line.
offline/** -text
